  "$id": "https://ivrm.jp/contracts/herta-community-game-stats-read/v4",
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "description": "Producer Herta Studio; consumer server-only ivrm-web. POST /api/ivrm/community-game-stats/read. Key=HMAC-SHA256(IVRM_INTEGRATION_TOKEN,herta-community-game-stats-read-v1); signature=HMAC-SHA256(key,timestamp.eventId.POST.path.rawBody). Headers X-IVRM-Timestamp ISO, X-IVRM-Event-Id UUID, X-IVRM-Signature hex. Five-minute freshness, no query, max8192bytes. Signing is unchanged from v1 (the v1 purpose string remains the key-derivation domain separator); the contract version is negotiated by the signed request field version: absent or 1 returns exactly the v1 response (overviewResponse / userResponse), 2 returns the same game sections plus a required activity section (overviewResponseV2 / userResponseV2), 3 adds the insights sections and the game mode (overviewResponseV3 / userResponseV3 / gameResponse), and 4 adds the overview channels section and messageCharUnits on the user activity (overviewResponseV4 / userResponseV4); the game mode accepts version 3 or 4 with an unchanged shape. The source of truth stays Herta community_game_activity_daily for games and community_activity_daily for activity; ivrm-web relays each read and stores no copy (ivrm-web #1703 S1/S4b, Herta #998). Request range from/to is a JST local_date range. mode is optional and defaults to overview: overview returns meta.earliestDate (the guild-wide first observed date, not range-limited), the top 25 games by totalSeconds with playerCount, and the user ranking paginated by limit/offset (max 100, ordered by totalSeconds desc then discordUserId asc; each entry carries its topGameName). mode=user requires discordUserId (and overview forbids it) and returns that user's totalSeconds plus their top 25 games. The v2 activity section is built only from the community_activity_daily metrics voice_seconds, messages and online_seconds (reactions are excluded: accumulated too sparsely). messages counts only the messages the bot's Activity Rules counted (cooldown-filtered), never the guild's raw message total; voice_seconds is stay time in countable voice channels; online_seconds is presence time and is a reference total only. overview activity carries guild totals for the range (voiceSeconds, messageCount, onlineSeconds, plus voiceMemberCount / messageMemberCount distinct-user counts) and the voice and message rankings, paginated by the same limit/offset as the game ranking (ordered by value desc then discordUserId asc). user activity carries only that user's voiceSeconds, messageCount and onlineSeconds for the range. Activity is fail-soft per section: when the activity read fails, activity is null while the game sections still return ok. All members are returned; opt-out filtering is applied by the ivrm-web relay, not here. Items carry aggregated seconds/counts only: no Rich Presence details/state, no message content, no raw session rows. All responses private,no-store. Version 3 returns the v2 sections plus a required insights section on overview and user, and unlocks mode=game (version 3 only). Overview insights carry the period totals (totalSeconds and distinct playerCount), a member-by-game matrix over the period's top 15 games (games ordered by totalSeconds desc then name asc; members ordered by their period total desc then discordUserId asc; secondsByGame aligns with games and zero-fills games a member did not play), the weekday distribution of play seconds as a Monday-first array of 7, and momentum for the same top 15 games (recentSeconds inside the trailing 7 days of the range, and newPlayerCount of players whose first observed play of that game falls inside the range). User insights carry playDays inside the range, longestStreakDays and currentStreakDays computed over the whole observed history up to the range end (streaks are personal-panel data only and are never ranked), lastPlayDate, the daily series inside the range (days without play are omitted), and the user's Monday-first weekday distribution. mode=game requires gameName and returns that game's totals with first/last observed play dates inside the range, every player's seconds paginated by limit/offset (ordered by totalSeconds desc then discordUserId asc), and viewer (null unless discordUserId is given): the viewer's competition rank over all players (null when the viewer has no play of the game in the range) and totalSeconds; the relay recomputes the viewer rank after opt-out filtering. Insights are fail-soft per section like activity: when an insights read fails, insights is null while the other sections still return ok; the game mode is a main content and fails with 503 instead. A game with no play inside the range returns zeroed game totals with null dates and an empty players list. Version 4 (ivrm-web #2035 S6, Herta #1054): the overview gains a required channels section, fail-soft like activity and insights (null when its read fails, while the other sections still return ok). channels.recordedFrom is the guild-wide first date of community_activity_channel_daily (not range-limited, null when the table holds no row for the guild); channel recording starts later than the activity totals, so the channel sums deliberately do not add up to the activity totals and consumers must say so. channels.voiceChannels and channels.messageChannels are the top 25 channels of the range by voice_seconds / messages from community_activity_channel_daily, each with memberCount (distinct users with a row in that channel). Channel names are not stored in the database: name is resolved by Studio from the bot guild options and is null when the channel no longer resolves (deleted, or the bot unreachable); a name is never invented, and consumers fall back to an id-derived label. channels.charUnits carries the message_char_units totals and the member ranking paginated like the other rankings. message_char_units is the bot's character-points metric: one unit per half-width (ASCII) character and two units per full-width character, excluding URLs, custom emoji, Unicode emoji and whitespace; points are units / 2, and the wire carries raw integer units only. The v4 user activity (activityUserV4) adds the user's own messageCharUnits to the three v2 fields; the v2/v3 activity shapes are unchanged.",
  "oneOf": [
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/overviewResponse"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/userResponse"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/overviewResponseV2"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/userResponseV2"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/overviewResponseV3"
    },
